# The Village of Barovia's few people indoors by day (lane 29, the interiors sweep, owner 2026-10-08: "some buildings
# could use a few more random people to make more lively"): a customer at Bildrath's, and two who still pray in the
# church. Unvoiced until the voice thread casts them.

~ shopper
if flag.viorica_candle
Goodwife Viorica: The tallow burned clean all the way down, without a drop of grease spilled.
Goodwife Viorica [smile]: For a whole hour the corner by the Morninglord's window was warmer than the street.
-> shopper_menu
endif
Goodwife Viorica [afraid]: Three coppers for a candle. Three. It was one, last spring. He says the roads are bad. The roads have always been bad.
-> shopper_menu

~ shopper_menu
* Do you need help? -> shopper_help
* [if not flag.viorica_secret_known] [Insight DC 12] (She keeps counting the same few coppers. Read her.) -> viorica_secret | viorica_secret_miss
* We'll leave you to it. -> END

~ shopper_help
Goodwife Viorica: Help? No. Nobody's ever helped by being seen helping in this village. Buy something, if you're buying. He watches who talks to whom.
if not flag.viorica_candle
Goodwife Viorica: Tallow was one copper in the spring, and now the board says three, though the sheep haven't grown any dearer.
* (Put a gold piece on the counter for the candle.) -> viorica_pay
endif
* Never mind. -> shopper_menu

~ viorica_pay
gold -1
set viorica_candle
Narrator: You set a gold piece on the scarred counter and nod toward the shelf of tallow dips.
Narrator: Bildrath does not look up from his ledger, writes a figure in the margin, and draws a single dry line through it.
Goodwife Viorica [afraid]: That is too much coin to leave on wood in this village. Put the rest back in your purse.
Goodwife Viorica: I only wanted the one, and perhaps a second in case the draught by the door blows the wick out.
Goodwife Viorica [sad]: Tomorrow is my boy's name-day. Eight years since he was christened, and two since the fever.
approve liriel_dawnsong +1 godrick_pendlebrook +1: You paid for a mother's candle
-> shopper_menu

~ viorica_secret
set viorica_secret_known
Goodwife Viorica [sad]: You have quiet eyes. Most folk who come through the gates look at us as if we are already ghosts.
Goodwife Viorica: These two coppers are what we took off my husband's eyelids before the sexton closed the box.
Goodwife Viorica [weary]: I cannot give them to Bildrath. I only bring them in to hear them clink on the counter, so I know what two sounds like.
-> shopper_menu

~ viorica_secret_miss
Narrator: Her expression gives nothing away at all. She slides the same few coppers back into a neat pile and counts them again.
-> shopper_menu

~ mihai
if quest.florins_grandson == done and flag.florin_told != "lie"
-> vallaki/florins_grandson:florin_after
endif
if flag.burgomaster_buried
Old Florin: They buried Kolyan properly. I prayed for him too. I'd not have, a year ago. You find the list gets longer as you get older, and less fussy.
-> mihai_menu
endif
Old Florin: My grandson went up the road to the castle to ask for work. That was two winters ago. I don't pray he comes back. I pray he doesn't.
* [if not quest.florins_grandson] Tell us about your grandson. -> vallaki/florins_grandson:florin_ask
* [if quest.florins_grandson == found] We found Tudorel. -> vallaki/florins_grandson:florin_choice
* We're sorry. -> END
* Why come here, if the priest can't help? -> mihai_why

~ mihai_menu
* [if not quest.florins_grandson] Tell us about your grandson. -> vallaki/florins_grandson:florin_ask
* [if quest.florins_grandson == found] We found Tudorel. -> vallaki/florins_grandson:florin_choice
* Goodbye. -> END

~ mihai_why
Old Florin: The roof keeps the rain off and the Morninglord keeps His opinions to Himself. That's more than I get at home.
-> END

~ sorina
if flag.doru_destroyed or flag.doru_freed
Goodwife Sorina: It's quiet under the floor now. Father Donavich says to give thanks. I'm giving them. I'm also keeping one eye on the door.
-> sorina_menu
endif
Goodwife Sorina: Shh. Father Donavich is praying, and when he stops the noise starts again from under the floor. Pray if you're staying. Or go, quietly.
-> sorina_menu

~ sorina_menu
* [if not flag.sorina_doru_known] Who do you pray for, besides the priest? -> sorina_ask
* Goodbye. -> END

~ sorina_ask
Goodwife Sorina [weary]: The usual list. The dead, the missing, the roof, the cabbages, and Father Donavich's knees. Not in that order.
Goodwife Sorina: When you have been on the bench an hour, you start throwing in the neighbours' goats just to fill the quiet.
* [Persuasion DC 11] You said the list was usual. Is anyone on it who isn't? -> sorina_told | sorina_shy
* Of course. -> sorina_menu

~ sorina_told
set sorina_doru_known
Goodwife Sorina [sad]: His boy, Doru. He had good hands for mending latches, and he used to whistle by our gate when he had no business on our lane.
Goodwife Sorina [weary]: He went up the castle road with a poker and a prayer, to put an end to it.
Goodwife Sorina [sad]: I think he wanted someone to watch him go. I watched. I've been praying ever since that it was enough.
-> sorina_menu

~ sorina_shy
Goodwife Sorina [weary]: Best I keep to my knees while the candle holds, stranger.
Goodwife Sorina: If the frost takes the cabbages tonight, there won't be enough left to boil on Sunday.
-> sorina_menu
